        "title": "Behavioral Finance Kya Hai — Introduction (Part 2)",
        "content": "1. **System 1 (Fast Brain)** — Automatically kaam karta hai, emotions se, bina soche\n2. **System 2 (Slow Brain)** — Soch-vichar ke kaam karta hai, logically\n\nProblem yeh hai ki **paise ke decisions mein hamara System 1 zyada active hota hai**. Jab tum mall mein jaate ho aur \"50% OFF\" ka board dekhte ho, toh turant khareedne ka mann karta hai — yeh System 1 hai. Jab sochte ho \"kya mujhe sach mein zaroorat hai?\" — yeh System 2 hai.\n\n**Real Example:**\nRahul ko pata hai ki uska monthly budget ₹5,000 hai. But jab Amazon pe \"Great Indian Festival\" aata hai, toh woh sochta hai — \"Yaar, itna discount kab milega!\" aur ₹15,000 kharch kar deta hai. Baad mein credit card bill dekh ke depression mein jaata hai.\n\n### India Ki Financial Literacy Ki Haalat\n\n| Statistic | Data |\n|-----------|------|\n| Financial Literacy Rate | 27% (only!) |\n| People who invest in stock market | ~5% of population |\n| Credit card default rate | ~3-4% annually |\n| Average savings rate | Declining from 30% to 18% |\n| People with emergency fund | Less than 15% |",
