        "cardIndex": 1,
        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Cognitive Biases Jo Tumhe Bechaare Banate Hain",
        "content": "Bhai, yeh sabse important section hai. **Cognitive biases** hamare dimag ki glitches hain jo humein galat decisions le parasti hain. Inko samjho toh life easy ho jaayegi!\n\n### 12 Cognitive Biases — Detailed Breakdown\n\n#### 1. Anchoring Bias (Ankur Bias)\n\n**Definition:** Pehla number jo tumne dekha woh anchor ban jaata hai aur baaki decisions usse affect hote hain.\n\n**How it affects money:**\nMRP dekh ke discount calculate karna — \"₹1000 ka tha, ₹500 mein mil raha hai, 50% off!\" But kya tumhe sach mein ₹500 ki cheez chahiye thi?\n\n**Indian Example:**\n\n| Product | MRP | Selling Price | \"Discount\" | Actual Value |\n|---------|-----|---------------|------------|--------------|\n| T-shirt | ₹1,999 | ₹999 | 50% off! | ₹300 worth fabric |\n| Watch | ₹5,000 | ₹2,500 | 50% off! | ₹800 worth mechanism |\n| Headphones | ₹3,000 | ₹1,499 | 50% off! | ₹600 worth sound |\n\nPriya ne ek \"₹5,000 ka bag\" ₹2,000 mein khareeda. Usko laga bahut savings hui. But actual mein bag ₹800 ka tha — ₹2,000 bhi zyada tha!\n\n**How to overcome:**\n- Socho: \"Kya main is cheez ko bina discount ke khareedta?\"\n- Actual value calculate karo, discount se nahi\n- \"Discount\" word ignore karo — price dekho, percentage nahi\n\n---\n\n#### 2. Loss Aversion (Haan Nuksan Wala Bias)\n\n**Definition:** Haan ka nuksan (loss) sukoon ka faayda (gain) se 2-2.5 zyada feel hota hai.\n\n**How it affects money:**\n- ₹100 ka nuksan dekh ke 2.5x zyada bura lagta hai jabki ₹100 ka faayda utna accha nahi lagta\n- Isliye log risky investments nahi karte, even agar expected return zyada ho\n- Isliye log loss pe stock bechte nahi, hold karte rehte hain\n\n**Indian Example:**\nAmit ne ₹10,000 lagaye stock market mein. Price ₹12,000 ho gayi (₹2,000 profit). Phir ₹9,000 ho gayi (₹1,000 loss). Ab woh hold kar raha hai kyunki \"sell karne pe loss confirm ho jaayega.\" Baad mein ₹6,000 ho gaya — ₹4,000 ka real loss!\n\n**The Math:**\n| Scenario | Feeling | Action |\n|----------|---------|--------|\n| ₹100 profit | 😊 Happy (level 1) | Sell kar lo! |\n| ₹100 loss | 😢 Very sad (level 2.5) | Hold karte hain... |\n\n**How to overcome:**\n- Pre-decide karo: \"10% loss pe sell karunga\"\n- Portfolio dekho, ek stock nahi\n- Emotional decisions mat lo — rules banao\n\n---\n\n#### 3. Herd Mentality (Bhed Chal)\n\n**Definition:** Jo sab kar rahe hain woh karo, bina soche.\n\n**How it affects money:**\n- Sab iPhone khareed rahe hain toh main bhi khareedunga\n- Sab crypto mein invest kar rahe hain toh main bhi karunga\n- Sab flat khareed rahe hain toh main bhi karunga\n\n**Indian Example:**\n\n| Year | Trend | Result |\n|------|-------|--------|\n| 2021 | Crypto boom | Log ne loan leke invest kiya, 80% ka paisa dooba |\n| 2022 | Real estate boom | Choti cities mein bhi prices badhe, buyers phas gaye |\n| 2023 | IPO craze | Many IPOs flop, retail investors loss mein |\n| 2024 | AI stocks | Valuations overinflated |\n\nKunal ne sab dost ke saath ek IPO mein ₹50,000 lagaye. Sabne bola \"yeh toh rocket hai!\" IPO listing pe 20% neeche aaya. 6 mahine baad 40% neeche hai. Kunal ka ₹50,000 ₹30,000 reh gaya.\n\n**How to overcome:**\n- Socho: \"Kya main akela yeh decision leta?\"\n- Research karo, trend nahi\n- Contrarian soch — \"sab khareed rahe hain toh shayad overpriced hai\"\n\n---\n\n#### 4. Confirmation Bias (Sahmati Bias)\n\n**Definition:** Sirf woh information padhna jo tumhari existing belief ko support kare.\n\n**How it affects money:**\n- Tumne ek stock khareeda hai — ab sirf positive news padh rahe ho\n- Tumhe lagta hai real estate best hai — sirf real estate ke benefits dekh rahe ho\n- Tum credit card ke khilaf ho — credit card ke benefits nahi dekh rahe\n\n**Indian Example:**\nRahul ne ₹1 lakh ek startup mein invest kiya. Ab woh sirf us startup ke positive articles padhta hai. Negative reviews dekh ke sochta hai \"yeh log jealous hain.\" 6 mahine baad startup band ho gaya. Rahul ko pata tha but usne reality nahi dekhi.\n\n**How to overcome:**\n- Intentionally opposite view padho\n- Ek friend ko bolo jo tumhare decision ko challenge kare\n- Decision journal maintain karo (Module 12.9 mein)",
