        "title": "Cognitive Biases Jo Tumhe Bechaare Banate Hain (Part 2)",
        "content": "---\n\n#### 5. Recency Bias (Haal Ka Bias)\n\n**Definition:** Jo recent mein hua woh future mein bhi hoga — yeh assume karna.\n\n**How it affects money:**\n- Last month stock market up hua — sochte hain future mein bhi up hoga\n- Pichle 3 saal se rent badh raha hai — sochte hain hamesha badhega\n- Ek scheme mein 3 month profit hua — lagate hain hamesha profit hoga\n\n**Indian Example:**\nMutual Fund X ne last 3 years mein 25% annual return diya. Priya ne socha \"25% toh mil raha hai!\" aur ₹2 lakh invest kiye. Next year market correction aaya, fund ne -10% diya. Priya shocked — \"yeh toh possible nahi tha!\"\n\n**How to overcome:**\n- Historical average dekho, recent performance nahi\n- Diversify karo (Module 7 cross-reference)\n- \"Past performance is not indicative of future results\" yaad rakho\n\n---\n\n#### 6. Endowment Effect (Apna Wala Bias)\n\n**Definition:** Jo cheez tumhare paas hai uski zyada value tumhe lagti hai.\n\n**How it affects money:**\n- Purana phone bechna mushkil lagta hai even agar naya chahiye\n- Apne shares bechna mushkil lagta hai even agar overvalued hain\n- Old course sell karna mushkil lagta hai even agar use nahi kar rahe\n\n**Indian Example:**\nAmit ke paas ek purana laptop hai jo ₹15,000 ka hai market mein. Woh sochta hai \"yeh toh ₹40,000 ka tha, main ₹25,000 mein toh doonga.\" But koi ₹15,000 se zyada nahi dega. Woh sell nahi kar pata aur naya laptop khareed nahi pata.\n\n**How to overcome:**\n- Socho: \"Agar yeh mere paas nahi hota, kitne mein khareedta?\"\n- Market price accept karo\n- Emotion alag karo reality se\n\n---\n\n#### 7. Sunk Cost Fallaya (Dooba Hua Paisa Ka Bias)\n\n**Definition:** \"Maine already itna paisa time laga diya hai, ab chhod nahi sakta.\"\n\n**How it affects money:**\n- Movie boring hai but \"paisa diya hai\" toh dekh rahe hain\n- Course useful nahi hai but \" ₹10,000 lagaye hain\" toh kar rahe hain\n- Stock loss mein hai but \"average down karunga\"\n\n**Indian Example:**\n\n| Scenario | Sunk Cost | Right Decision |\n|----------|-----------|----------------|\n| Boring movie | ₹200 ticket | Movie chhod do, ₹200 toh gaye |\n| Useless course | ₹10,000 fee | Course chhod do, ₹10,000 toh gaye |\n| Bad stock | ₹50,000 invested | Sell karo, ₹50,000 toh gaye |\n| Bad relationship | 3 years invested | Move on, 3 years toh gaye |\n\nSneha ne ₹8,000 ek online course ke liye diye. 2 lectures dekh ke samajh aaya ki course bekaar hai. But usne socha \"paisa toh gaya, kuch toh seekho.\" 2 mahine waste kiye aur woh bhi bekaar.\n\n**How to overcome:**\n- Socho: \"Agar abhi free mein milta, toh kya karta?\"\n- Future cost-benefit karo, past nahi\n- \"Paisa gaya\" accept karo, move on karo\n\n---\n\n#### 8. Present Bias (Aaj Ka Bias)\n\n**Definition:** Aaj ka sukoon kal ke faayde se zyada important lagta hai.\n\n**How it affects money:**\n- Aaj party karenge, kal se save karenge\n- Aaj khareedenge, kal EMI bharenge\n- Aaj enjoy karenge, kal invest karenge\n\n**Indian Example:**\nKunal ka monthly budget:\n| Item | Budgeted | Actual | Reason |\n|------|----------|--------|--------|\n| Food | ₹3,000 | ₹5,000 | \"Aaj doston ke saath jaana tha\" |\n| Entertainment | ₹1,000 | ₹3,000 | \"New movie release tha\" |\n| Shopping | ₹2,000 | ₹6,000 | \"Sale tha yaar!\" |\n| Savings | ₹4,000 | ₹0 | \"Kal se pakka!\" |\n\n**Calculation:**\nAgar Kunal har month ₹4,000 save karta aur 12% return milta:\n| Duration | Amount Saved | With Returns |\n|----------|-------------|--------------|\n| 1 year | ₹48,000 | ₹50,160 |\n| 5 years | ₹2,40,000 | ₹2,94,586 |\n| 10 years | ₹4,80,000 | ₹9,21,024 |\n\nAb Kunal \"aaj ka maza\" le raha hai, but ₹9.21 lakh future mein lose kar raha hai!\n\n**How to overcome:**\n- Auto-debit setup karo (Module 12.7)\n- \"Pay yourself first\" rule lagao\n- Visual reminders lagao — \"10 years baad kya hoga?\"\n\n---\n\n#### 9. Mental Accounting (Dimag Ka Hisab)",
