        "cardIndex": 2,
        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Emotional Spending Triggers — Kab Kharch Kar Dete Ho Bina Soche (Part 2)",
        "content": "**Indian Example:**\nSneha ka result aaya — 1st division! Usne socha \"Party deni chahiye!\" ₹8,000 kharch kiye dinner pe. Ab uska monthly budget bigad gaya. 2 mahine tak guilt feel kar rahi thi.\n\n---\n\n#### 5. Sadness Spending (Breakup Shopping)\n\n| Aspect | Details |\n|--------|---------|\n| **Trigger** | Breakup, rejection, loneliness, bad news |\n| **Warning Signs** | \"Khud ko khush karne ke liye kuch khareedta hoon\" |\n| **Common Purchases** | Comfort food, clothes, gadgets |\n| **Prevention Strategy** | Emotional awareness, support system |\n| **Alternative Action** | Talk to friend, exercise, creative outlet |\n\n**Indian Example:**\nPriya ka breakup hua. Usne ₹10,000 kharch kiye — naye kapde, makeup, spa. \"Khud ko treat kar rahi hoon.\" 1 mahine baad bank balance dekh ke royi.\n\n---\n\n#### 6. FOMO Spending (Sale Ends Today!)\n\n| Aspect | Details |\n|--------|---------|\n| **Trigger** | Limited time offers, \"last few hours\" |\n| **Warning Signs** | \"Abhi nahi kiya toh miss ho jaayega!\" |\n| **Common Purchases** | Anything on sale, flash deals |\n| **Prevention Strategy** | \"24-hour rule\" lagao |\n| **Alternative Action** | Socho: \"Agar kal bhi ye deal hoti, tab bhi khareedta?\" |\n\n**Indian Example:**\nAmazon Great Indian Festival — \"2 hours left!\" Kunal ne ₹15,000 ka smartwatch khareed liya. Actually use watch chahiye thi but ₹5,000 ki. ₹10,000 extra \"discount\" ke chakkar mein kharch kiye.\n\n---\n\n#### 7. Comparison Spending (Padosi Ka Naya Phone)\n\n| Aspect | Details |\n|--------|---------|\n| **Trigger** | Social media, neighbors, colleagues |\n| **Warning Signs** | \"Uske paas hai, mujhe kyun nahi?\" |\n| **Common Purchases** | Gadgets, clothes, car, house |\n| **Prevention Strategy** | Social media limit, gratitude practice |\n| **Alternative Action** | \"Unfollow\" karo, apna progress track karo |\n\n**Indian Example:**\nAmit ke dost ne naya iPhone khareeda. Amit ka phone 6 mahine purana hai but ab lagta hai \"purana hai.\" Usne bhi iPhone khareed liya — ₹80,000. EMI ₹5,000/month for 16 months. Ab stress mein hai.\n\n---\n\n#### 8. Reward Spending (Mehnat Ki, Khareed Lo)\n\n| Aspect | Details |\n|--------|---------|\n| **Trigger** | Task complete, hard work, achievement |\n| **Warning Signs** | \"Iska reward chahiye!\" |\n| **Common Purchases** | Treats, gadgets, experiences |\n| **Prevention Strategy** | Non-monetary rewards plan karo |\n| **Alternative Action** | Self-care (exercise, nature, friends) |",
